<h1>Rules</h1>

<h2>Study rooms</h2>
<ul class="rules">
  <li>These group study rooms are located at the North Oshawa Library</li>
  <li>Your student ID can only be used once per day to a maximum of 20 bookings per term.</li>
  <li>Bookings are available for a maximum of 3 hours per day</li>
  <li>Bookings can be made up to a week in advance and can be cancelled up to 24 hours before the booking start time.</li>
  <li>New booking dates are added at 9 a.m. each day.</li>
  <li>Bookings cannot be created five minutes before the start time </li>
  <li>If you cancel your reservation, you may re-use your student ID to create a booking for the same day</li>
</ul>

<h2>Lab equipment</h2>
<ul class="rules">
  <li>Equipment is for coursework and practice by students in networking and computer science/ engineering courses.</li>
  <li>Equipment stays in its lab. Cables in the networking lab are specially designated for networking lab use.</li>
  <li>You CAN remove or add cables to fit your topology but they must be returned to their designated places after use.</li>
  <li>Before you leave, erase and reload your device configurations, return cables back to their places if used.</li>
  <li>Report anything damaged or missing to the TAs or professor right away.</li>
</ul>

